food/drinks are heavenly. My boyfriend and I decided to split a bunch of things from the menu instead of ordering our own entrees an..."},{"business_id":"I0I2mkCOPTYVSLpc8A8VVw","review_id":"8O2nXfuKSCPlllLHSp6kxg","date":"2015-07-14T07:14:36","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9420879483222961,"text_excerpt":"Best meal I've had in a looong time. Flavors are bold, pacing is perfect, and clearly attention is focused on details to give diners the experience they hope to get from a place like this. All staff members were kind, professional, and inviting. I arrived before my friends so I had a drink at the bar which I'd recommend. It's amazing to watch the mixologists work their magic, they have a very unique cocktail list (delicious!). The meal started with biscuits with bacon butter, I just wish they served most than chiclet of butte. The croquettes were a fun taste explosion as well. They taste of cheese but the server assured us no cheese is inside. We also got the tuna which was excellent, did..."},{"business_id":"I0I2mkCOPTYVSLpc8A8VVw","review_id":"h2NStEOJZF9lhPHWLy65mg","date":"2015-06-15T17:51:20","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9396418333053589,"text_excerpt":"It's been a while since I've tried somewhere new, so with a friend moving to Chicago, this was the perfect occasion. We decided on Compere Lapin, Nina Lacompe's new restaurant. Chef Lacompte is a recent runner up of Top Chef. Her background and influence is mostly Caribbean, so I was excited to try what I thought would be some interesting flavors. I wasn't disappointed. Atmosphere: A- I loved the atmosphere. Rich browns, interesting lighting, exposed brick. Had a prohibition era type feel to it. I did find it to get pretty loud at times. They should probably invest in some cushioning underneath the tables. Service: B+ This is a tough one to rate. This is a new restaurant, and they're tryi..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"I0I2mkCOPTYVSLpc8A8VVw","photo_id":"DgsfZmj8ZYUtrZW5p59fWw","label":"inside